 80: ```
 81: 
 82: ---
 83: 
 84: ## Services
 85: 
 86: ### Infrastructure
 87: 
 88: | Service | Image | Port | Description |
 89: |---|---|---|---|
 90: | **PostgreSQL** | `postgres:16-alpine` | 5432 | Primary database — orders, products, events, notifications, inventory |
 91: | **Redis** | `redis:7-alpine` | 6379 | Cache layer — product catalog (TTL 60s) |
 92: | **Kafka** | `apache/kafka:3.7.0` | 9092 | Event streaming platform — KRaft mode (no ZooKeeper) |
 93: | **Kafka Exporter** | `danielqsj/kafka-exporter` | 9308 | Exports Kafka metrics → Prometheus |
 94: | **Kafka UI** | `provectuslabs/kafka-ui` | 8585 | Web UI for Kafka topic/consumer inspection |
 95: 
 96: ### Application Services
 97: 
 98: | Service | Port | Description |
 99: |---|---|---|
100: | **Web UI** | 8580 | Nginx SPA — dashboard, orders, events, load testing |
101: | **API Gateway** | 5000 | BFF pattern — routes, aggregates, error propagation |
102: | **Order Service** | 5001 | Create orders, manage payments, publish Kafka events |
103: | **Payment Service** | 5002 | Simulated payment processing with configurable latency/errors |
104: | **Traffic Generator** | 5003 | Load testing tool with scenario templates (flash sale, pipeline) |
105: | **Notification Worker** | 5004 | Kafka consumer — processes order events → sends notifications |
106: | **Inventory Worker** | 5005 | Kafka consumer — processes order events → manages stock |
107: 
108: ### Observability Stack (Separate VM)
109: 
110: | Tool | Port | Description |
111: |---|---|---|
112: | **OTel Collector** | 4317/4318 | Receives OTLP traces/metrics/logs, routes to backends |
113: | **Prometheus** | 9090 | Metrics storage, PromQL, recording rules, alerting rules |
114: | **Grafana** | 3000 | Dashboards — application health, Kafka, workers, SLO |
115: | **Tempo** | 3200 | Distributed tracing backend |
116: | **Loki** | 3100 | Log aggregation with LogQL |
117: | **Alertmanager** | 9093 | Alert routing → Telegram |
118: | **Blackbox Exporter** | 9115 | Active probing — HTTP health checks to service `/health/live` endpoints |
119: 
120: ---
121: 
122: ## Data Flow
123: 
124: ### Synchronous (HTTP Request Path)
125: ```
126: Web UI → API Gateway → Order Service → Payment Service
127:                               ↕              
128:                          PostgreSQL     
129:                               ↕              
130:                            Redis (cache)
131: ```
132: 
133: ### Asynchronous (Event-Driven Path)
134: ```
135: Order Service ──publish──► Kafka (topic: order.events)
136:                                │
137:                     ┌──────────┴──────────┐
138:                     ▼                     ▼
139:            Notification Worker     Inventory Worker
140:            (group: notif-workers)  (group: inv-workers)
141:                     │                     │
142:                     ▼                     ▼
143:               notifications         inventory_log
144:               (PostgreSQL)          (PostgreSQL)
145: ```
146: 
147: ### Kafka Event Types
148: 
149: | Event | Trigger | Consumed By |
150: |---|---|---|
151: | `order.created` | New order saved | Notification Worker, Inventory Worker |
152: | `order.payment_completed` | Payment success | Notification Worker |
153: | `order.payment_failed` | Payment rejected | Notification Worker, Inventory Worker |
154: | `stock.depleted` | Stock insufficient (< threshold) | Inventory Worker (triggers auto-restock) |
155: 
156: ### Telemetry Pipeline
157: ```
158: All Services ──OTLP gRPC──► OTel Collector ──► Prometheus (metrics)
159:                                             ──► Tempo (traces)
160:                                             ──► Loki (logs)
161:                                             ──► Grafana (dashboards)
162: 
163: Blackbox Exporter ──probe /health/live──► Application Services
164: Prometheus ──scrape──► Blackbox Exporter (probe results)
165: ```
166: 
167: ---
168: 
169: ## Database Schema
170: 
171: ```mermaid
172: erDiagram
173:     orders {
174:         serial id PK
175:         varchar order_id UK
176:         integer product_id FK
177:         varchar product_name
178:         integer quantity
179:         decimal total_amount
180:         varchar status
181:         varchar payment_txn_id
182:         timestamp created_at
183:         timestamp updated_at
184:     }
185: 
186:     products {
187:         serial id PK
188:         varchar name
189:         decimal price
190:         integer stock
191:         varchar category
192:     }
193: 
194:     processed_events {
195:         varchar event_id PK
196:         varchar event_type
197:         varchar processed_by PK
198:         timestamp processed_at
199:     }
200: 
201:     notifications {
202:         serial id PK
