 823: ### Backup & Restore
 824: 
 825: ```bash
 826: # Backup per-database
 827: pg_dump -h localhost -U app_user app_db > backup/app_db_$(date +%Y%m%d).sql
 828: pg_dump -h localhost -U auth_user auth_db > backup/auth_db_$(date +%Y%m%d).sql
 829: pg_dump -h localhost -U shipping_user shipping_db > backup/shipping_db_$(date +%Y%m%d).sql
 830: 
 831: # Restore
 832: pg_restore -h localhost -U app_user -d app_db < backup/app_db_20250519.sql
 833: 
 834: # Verify backup integrity
 835: pg_restore --list backup/app_db_20250519.sql  # dry-run, no actual restore
 836: ```
 837: 
 838: - Backup schedule: daily (cron or Docker healthcheck trick)
 839: - Retention: 7 days local, rotate oldest
 840: - Verify: monthly restore drill to verify backups are usable
 841: - **RTO/RPO definitions:** RTO = 30 min (restore from backup), RPO = 24h (daily backup)
 842: 
 843: ### Log Rotation
 844: 
 845: ```yaml
 846: # docker-compose.yml — apply cho tất cả services
 847: services:
 848:   order-service:
 849:     logging:
 850:       driver: json-file
 851:       options:
 852:         max-size: "10m"
 853:         max-file: "3"
 854: ```
 855: 
 856: **Tại sao:** Without log rotation, Docker logs grow unbounded → disk full → entire VM down.
